  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e7e6a7a7e46c14191819aae88fd283a2, type: 3}
  m_Name: New Dialog Data
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Dialog: "\"Honestly, this wine is incredible, but I think I\u2019m mostly just
    relieved to finally be sitting down. My day started at 5:00 AM, which is basically
    a crime against humanity.\n\nI woke up to Barnaby\u2014my Maine Coon, you remember
    him from my profile?\u2014sitting directly on my windpipe. He doesn't meow for
    food; he just stares at you until you feel your soul leaving your body. After
    I fed him his 'organic, hand-flaked' salmon, I tried to hop on a quick Zoom call
    with my mom.\n\nShe\u2019s lovely, truly, but she spent twenty minutes explaining
    why my brother\u2019s new tattoo is a 'sign of the apocalypse.' I love my family,
    but they treat every minor inconvenience like a Shakespearean tragedy. I finally
    hung up, grabbed my latte, and stepped outside, thinking it was just going to
    be another Tuesday.\n\nThen I saw the first one.\n\nA guy in full black shinobi
    gear was scaling the side of the Starbucks. People were just walking by, staring
    at their phones, totally oblivious to the silent coup happening on the rooftops.
    I realized then that the 'Ninja Revolution' I\u2019d seen rumored on the dark
    web wasn't a joke.\n\nThey were everywhere, dropping from the rafters, armed
    with smoke bombs and those little throwing stars. I couldn't just let them take
    over the city; I have a Pilates class on Thursdays that I\u2019ve already paid
    for.\n\nI didn't have a sword, but I did have a heavy-duty yoga mat and a very
    hot triple-shot espresso. It\u2019s amazing what you can do with high-tension
    rubber and caffeine when your adrenaline kicks in. I took out the lead scout
    with a well-timed sweep of my gym bag\u2014thank god for heavy lifting.\n\nI
    spent the next three hours parkouring across the financial district, dismantling
    their communications network. I actually had to use a hairpin to short-circuit
    their main EMP device near the pier. By the time the sun started to set, the
    Grand Master realized I wasn't backing down and called for a strategic retreat.\n\nI
    made it home just in time to see Barnaby had knocked my favorite vase off the
    counter. He looked at me with so much judgment, like he was saying, 'You\u2019re
    late with my treats, world-saver.'\n\nI did a quick load of laundry, scrubbed
    the soot off my forehead, and put on this dress. And now I\u2019m here!\n\nSo...
    that was my Tuesday. How was your day? Did you get those spreadsheets finished?\""
  RightAnswerReply: "A guy in full black shinobi gear was scaling the side of the
    Starbucks. People were just walking by, staring at their phones, totally oblivious
    to the silent coup happening on the rooftops. I realized then that the 'Ninja
    Revolution' I\u2019d seen rumored on the dark web wasn't a joke."
